Also, I would suggest DR DOS 6.0.  Each move under NH3.1 took about a second
or 2 on my machine, a 20 Mhz Harris 286 with 4 MB (2 MB as EMS --> Super-PC KWIK),
and was unbearable.  (O/S was MS DOS 3.3)

DR DOS freed up a lot of conventional mememory; I now have 619k free of the 640!
Moves take about half a second now normally, and up to a second when a large shop
or beehive is on the level.  Not superfast, but definately bearable.

Only headache was getting the memory manager to work.  I had to put the EMS driver
before it in my CONFIG.SYS; the installation program does the opposite and I hear`
this is a common "fix."

